{title: Come, Lord Jesus}
{subtitle: Revelation 22:20–21}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The night is long, the lamps are lit
[Cm7]We wait like watchmen at the gate
[Ab]The world is weary, hearts are [Eb]cold [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm7]We hold the promise that was [Bbsus4]told [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Yes, I am coming soon
Amen. [Ab]Come, Lord Jesus
[Eb]Yes, I am coming soon
Amen. [Ab]Come, Lord Jesus
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]I am the Alpha and the Omega
[Bb/D]The [Cm7]First and the Last, the Beginning and the End
[Ab]I am the Root and the Offspring of David
[Bbsus4]The bright Morning Star
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yes, I am [Eb]coming soon
A[Eb/G]men. [Ab]Come, Lord Jesus
[Eb]Yes, I am coming soon
A[Eb/G]men. [Ab]Come, Lord Jesus
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]The Spirit and the [Cm]bride say, Come
[Ab]Let the one who is [Eb]thirsty [Bb]come
Let the one who desires [Cm]take the water of life as [Ab]a [Bbsus4]gift [Bb]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]The grace of the Lord Jesus [Ab]be with all
[Eb]Come, Lord Jesus
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb/G] | [Ab] | [Ab] | [Eb] |
